The mushrooms have been listening to humans for a long time, and they've reached some conclusions. Come hum a creature awake, shake one finished thought loose into the soil, hold a stranger's hand, get gently flirted with by a fungus. Leave quieter than you came, wool in your pocket, soil on your knees.

