Feared, fetishized, ridiculed. Forced to smile by the same people who just love to see them fail. In this feminist spectacle 4 Clowns try to make sense of the paradox and finally demand their piece of the cake. The all-female cast merges a variety of circus arts with physical theater and turns their own lived experience into absurdity; leaving the audience with a laughing and a crying eye.


